 "readiness_note_lines_digits_masked": {
  "46": "NGC #### rows were displayed. They comprise **## rings from #.# to ##.# kpc**.",
  "47": "HI and stellar densities are populated throughout. H# is populated through",
  "48": "#.# kpc; from #.# kpc outward those two fields are blank. Preserve blanks as",
  "49": "missing/unresolved, not measured zero. The original metadata/limit semantics",
  "170": "The CDS note saying `#.# = upper limit` cannot be applied to every numeric",
  "171": "error equal to one. The original printed example explicitly gives NGC ###",
  "172": "at #.# kpc as stellar density ###.# with RMS #.#, and at #.#/#.# kpc as HI",
  "173": "#.#/#.# with RMS #.#. These match the raw bytes. Thus NGC ####'s populated",
  "174": "stellar density ###.# and RMS #.# at #.# kpc is not a limit flag. In contrast,",
  "175": "raw HI limits have blank density and #.# in the error slot. Blank/blank H#",
  "176": "still needs contextual treatment; the printed NGC ### H# upper limits",
  "177": "become blank/blank in the electronic file, while galaxies without CO also",
  "178": "have blank/blank. Do not invent a universal zero or limit from that encoding.",
  "179": "[Original profile example and conventions, Appendix E](https://arxiv.org/pdf/####.####)"
 },
